# 6. Core Offering Areas

These offering areas define VFXNOW's business context.

They are reference material and do **not** all need to appear in individual articles.

Specific availability and configurations may vary.

## 6.1 Workstations and Desktops

High-performance workstations designed for professional creative workloads.

These systems may support work such as:

* compositing
* 3D
* simulation
* editing
* rendering
* real-time production

Articles should not list workloads unless the distinction materially affects the hardware discussion.

## 6.2 Laptops

Portable systems configured for professional creative work when production requirements call for mobility alongside workstation-level capability.

The editorial focus should remain on the workload and configuration requirement rather than generic portability benefits.

## 6.3 Servers and Compute Nodes

Compute resources that can support rendering, processing, and other production workloads requiring capacity beyond individual artist workstations.

## 6.4 Storage Solutions

Storage hardware intended to support professional media and production environments.

Storage should be discussed in relation to the actual workload, throughput, capacity, or collaboration requirement rather than as a generic VFXNOW capability.

## 6.5 Monitors and Peripherals

Professional displays and related equipment for production environments where the peripheral itself materially affects the work.

## 6.6 Software-Ready Configurations

VFXNOW can provide systems configured around industry-standard creative software environments.

Relevant applications may include:

* Foundry Nuke
* Autodesk Maya
* Houdini
* Adobe Creative Cloud
* Flame
* Unreal Engine

These applications are reference examples.

Do not insert them into articles simply to demonstrate production familiarity.

Use a specific application only when its workload characteristics matter to the hardware decision being discussed.

